<title>USA: Black Warrior calls reorganizes.</title>
<headline>Black Warrior calls reorganizes.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Miss. 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Black Warrior Wireline Corp said it has exchanged $1,193,750 of debt and accrued interest for 691,875 common shares and five-year warrants to purchase 285,000 shares of the company's common stock at $2.00 per share as part of its ongoing reorganization plan.</p>
<p>The oil and gas well service company said its latest debt-for-equity conversion nearly completes the reorganization effort begun in 1995, when $1,353,382 of debt and interest were converted into 648,151 shares of common stock.</p>
<p>The company said there are about 1,500,000 shares issued and outstanding following the debt exchange.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
